    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dd194636"
      },
      "source": [
        "Now, let's create the Streamlit app. I'll save the code for the app in a Python file named `app.py`. You'll need to run this file from your terminal to launch the app."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "f38b2c80",
        "outputId": "032c2bc2-5e9c-4072-ce86-be6e0a926472"
      },
      "source": [
        "%%writefile app.py\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "import joblib\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load the trained model\n",
        "model = joblib.load('logi.sav')\n",
        "\n",
        "st.title('Delivery Delay Prediction App')\n",
        "st.write('Enter the details below to predict if there will be a delivery delay.')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Input fields for each feature\n",
        "delivery_distance = st.sidebar.number_input('Delivery Distance', min_value=0.0, value=19.35)\n",
        "traffic_congestion = st.sidebar.slider('Traffic Congestion (1-5)', 1, 5, 3)\n",
        "weather_condition = st.sidebar.slider('Weather Condition (1-5)', 1, 5, 3)\n",
        "delivery_slot = st.sidebar.slider('Delivery Slot (1-3)', 1, 3, 2)\n",
        "driver_experience = st.sidebar.number_input('Driver Experience (years)', min_value=0, value=10)\n",
        "num_stops = st.sidebar.number_input('Number of Stops', min_value=0, value=5)\n",
        "vehicle_age = st.sidebar.number_input('Vehicle Age (years)', min_value=0, value=5)\n",
        "road_condition_score = st.sidebar.slider('Road Condition Score (1-5)', 1, 5, 3)\n",
        "package_weight = st.sidebar.number_input('Package Weight (kg)', min_value=0.0, value=20.0)\n",
        "fuel_efficiency = st.sidebar.number_input('Fuel Efficiency (km/L)', min_value=0.0, value=15.0)\n",
        "warehouse_processing_time = st.sidebar.number_input('Warehouse Processing Time (minutes)', min_value=0, value=45)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create a DataFrame for prediction\n",
        "input_data = pd.DataFrame([[\n",
        "    delivery_distance,\n",
        "    traffic_congestion,\n",
        "    weather_condition,\n",
        "    delivery_slot,\n",
        "    driver_experience,\n",
        "    num_stops,\n",
        "    vehicle_age,\n",
        "    road_condition_score,\n",
        "    package_weight,\n",
        "    fuel_efficiency,\n",
        "    warehouse_processing_time\n",
        "]], columns=[\n",
        "    'Delivery_Distance', 'Traffic_Congestion', 'Weather_Condition',\n",
        "    'Delivery_Slot', 'Driver_Experience', 'Num_Stops', 'Vehicle_Age',\n",
        "    'Road_Condition_Score', 'Package_Weight', 'Fuel_Efficiency',\n",
        "    'Warehouse_Processing_Time'\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "if st.button('Predict Delivery Delay'):\n",
        "    prediction = model.predict(input_data)\n",
        "    prediction_proba = model.predict_proba(input_data)\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader('Prediction Result:')\n",
        "    if prediction[0] == 1:\n",
        "        st.error('**Delivery is likely to be Delayed!**')\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        st.success('**Delivery is likely to be On-Time.**')\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.write(f'Probability of No Delay: {prediction_proba[0][0]:.2f}')\n",
        "    st.write(f'Probability of Delay: {prediction_proba[0][1]:.2f}')\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": 24,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Writing app.py\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a69ca19e"
      },
      "source": [
        "To run this Streamlit app:\n",
        "\n",
        "1.  **Save the code:** You've already done this by running the `%%writefile app.py` cell.\n",
        "2.  **Open a terminal:** In Colab, you can do this by going to `File` > `New notebook` > `Open a new terminal` (or similar, depending on your Colab version). You might also be able to open a terminal directly in the notebook environment.\n",
        "3.  **Navigate to the directory** where `app.py` and `logi.sav` are saved (likely `/content/`).\n",
        "4.  **Run the app:** Execute the command: `streamlit run app.py`\n",
        "\n",
        "Streamlit will then provide you with a local URL and a network URL. Click on the network URL to open your app in a new browser tab."
      ]
    }
  ]
}